// a `}` at file scope closes a scope nothing opened. the body pass used to read it as the end of the
// root scope and stop, so everything below it was never parsed - no diagnostic, no output, and a clean
// exit status. the declaration pass walked straight past it, which is the disagreement: one pass saw
// the `echo` and the struct, the other saw neither
//
// reported and skipped now, so the two passes reach the same declarations and the file is refused

}

echo 1;

struct bar { usize $pos; }
